WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.940
LinkedIn locked me out for a bit a few months ago.

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:09.148
My crime: posting 3 TIMES in about 10 minutes.

00:00:08.898 --> 00:00:12.142
The system looked at that and decided:

00:00:11.892 --> 00:00:14.965
"No human WRITES THAT FAST."

00:00:14.715 --> 00:00:16.232
"Must be A BOT."

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:19.286
Here is what actually happened that morning.

00:00:19.036 --> 00:00:21.641
I had 3 ideas in my head.

00:00:21.391 --> 00:00:25.228
I talked them through with AI, by voice —

00:00:24.978 --> 00:00:30.681
thinking out loud, arguing back, rewriting as I went.

00:00:30.431 --> 00:00:34.865
The ideas were mine. The writing was mine.

00:00:34.615 --> 00:00:36.933
AI was A SPARRING PARTNER.

00:00:36.683 --> 00:00:40.628
By the time I sat down, all 3 were ready to post.

00:00:40.648 --> 00:00:45.435
Work that used to take HOURS took MINUTES.

00:00:45.455 --> 00:00:50.305
The way I see it, LinkedIn's spam filter is a model —

00:00:50.055 --> 00:00:54.250
and every model is trained on THE OLD WORLD'S data.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.810
In the old world, 3 real posts —

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:00.920
3 real posts in 10 minutes — MEANS A BOT.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:04.453
So the model looked at me and said: "BROKEN."

00:01:04.473 --> 00:01:06.725
But the model is what's BROKEN DOWN.

00:01:06.745 --> 00:01:09.477
And the models like this are EVERYWHERE.

00:01:09.227 --> 00:01:12.001
Your org runs on them, too.

00:01:12.021 --> 00:01:19.094
Approval chains, review cycles, meeting cadence, planning timelines —

00:01:18.844 --> 00:01:22.870
all trained on how fast a human USED TO work.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.750
So here is my working theory:

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:29.540
The rules were trained on OLD DATA.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:31.381
AI just CHANGED THE DATA.

00:01:31.131 --> 00:01:36.741
You don't argue with a stale model — you RETRAIN it.

00:01:36.491 --> 00:01:41.900
So which of your models is still running on OLD DATA?
